Host-side gtest unit tests for crosspoint-reader.

Build and run:

  cmake -S test -B build/test
  cmake --build build/test
  ctest --test-dir build/test --output-on-failure -j

Run a single suite directly:

  cmake --build build/test --target StreamingJsonParserTest
  build/test/streaming_json_parser/StreamingJsonParserTest --gtest_filter='*'

Google Test is fetched via CMake FetchContent on first configure; the pinned
version lives in test/CMakeLists.txt.

map_transfer covers the BLE transfer receiver's decisions -- the frame parse,
the begin refusal ladder and the chunk state machine, lifted out of
MapTransferReceiver.cpp so the host can reach them at all. A new refusal or gate
goes in src/activities/map/MapTransferDecide.h (T-2106; the parent repo's
docs/ble-map-transfer-protocol.md has the why).

gnss_sky_view covers the satellite wait screen's projection: azimuth and
elevation to a pixel, the signal buckets and the mountain ridge profile
(docs/gnss-acquire.md).

Three targets here are host tools, not gtest suites, so ctest does not run them:

  map_preview  renders a map frame with the device's own MapRenderer --
               docs/device-preview.md (parent repo)
  map_replay   replays a recorded ride through the device's own
               MapFollow::decide() and counts redraws, with a threshold sweep
               -- docs/map-follow.md, "Sweeping the thresholds off the device"
  wallet_preview
               renders a generated wallet asset through the device's own
               WalletAsset/ManifestParser code and writes PNGs of the
               framebuffer -- docs/wallet-viewer.md, "Read against real
               generator output". `pio run -t wallet-preview`.
               `--code N` renders a machine-readable code and reports its hash,
               module box, centring and label band -- same doc, "The code
               screen". `--key <64 hex>` renders an ENCRYPTED tree: GCM tag
               first, then AES-256-CTR per asset -- docs/wallet-crypto.md.
               `--grey` renders the level's grey asset as four visible levels,
               cross-checks the baked planes against the 2bpp image, and writes
               <out>-capture.bin -- the exact CMD:SCREENSHOT_GRAY payload for that
               window, which tools/greyshot.py decodes off-device;
               `--synth-grey DIR` writes a synthetic grey tree to render --
               docs/wallet-grey.md
  map_window   the map screen at 480x800 in an SDL2 window: a replayed ride or
               a position you choose, the real decisions and the real renderer
               together, a menu for rungs/modes/layers, and the map module's own
               log -- docs/map-follow.md, "map_window"

map_window needs SDL2 (`apt install libsdl2-dev`). Without it CMake skips that
one target and everything else still configures.

These live in test/build/, which is gitignored -- so a worktree that is removed
takes its binaries with it. Rebuild in whichever checkout you are using:

  cmake -S test -B test/build && cmake --build test/build --target map_window

A new file under src/ that a *shared* unit calls -- MapRenderer,
MapPreviewPipeline, anything several suites link -- must be added to **every**
test target that links that unit, not only to the new suite's own
CMakeLists.txt. The symptom is a link error that reads like a missing
implementation:

  undefined reference to `MapPointSource::MapPointSource(IFileSource&, ...)'

MapTileReaderGoldenTest stopped linking when the point layer landed, because
test/map_tile_reader/CMakeLists.txt never gained MapPointReader.cpp,
MapPointSource.cpp and MapPointMarks.cpp while MapRenderer.cpp started calling
into them. Fixed 2026-08-22. Grep the new file's class name across
test/*/CMakeLists.txt after adding one.
